# In-Game `/agent` Command

Players with `neighborhood.agent` (default: OP) run:

```text
/agent <prompt>
/agent confirm <token> <prompt>
```

## Architecture

1. **Paper plugin** `NeighborhoodAgent` in `mc-lan` POSTs to the orchestrator.
2. **Orchestrator** Compose service `mc-agent` (private network, no host port).
   Source: `agent/orchestrator/app.py`. Entrypoint: `python -m agent.orchestrator`.
3. **Models**:
   - Local Ollama first (default `qwen2.5:7b-instruct`); bounded
     `qwen3:8b` fallback.
   - Cloud fallback when `OPENAI_API_KEY` is set
     (`CLOUD_BASE_URL` / `CLOUD_MODEL`).
   - Ollama may be on the host (`OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434`)
     or bundled (`OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://ollama:11434` + `COMPOSE_PROFILES=ollama`
     in `.env`). `make bootstrap` writes both for you.
4. **Tools**: same `agent/tools/` package + `agent/tool_registry.py` as the
   Cursor MCP — never duplicate logic in Java.
5. **Smart context** (per request): `agent/context.py` injects online players,
   time of day, player facing, and recent agent actions; `agent/retrieval.py`
   pulls relevant chunks from `agent/knowledge/{blocks,fawe,patterns}.md`.
6. **Thinking-mode models** (qwen3, deepseek-r1, qwq) get `/no_think`,
   `think: false`, and short local timeouts — required for valid tool-call JSON.
7. **Prompt-mode tool fallback**: families that don't support Ollama's native
   `tools` API (e.g. `deepseek-r1`) get tool schemas inlined in the system
   prompt and return JSON we parse with `_extract_prompt_tool_call`. They also
   get a longer timeout floor — see `_NO_NATIVE_TOOLS_FAMILIES` in
   `agent/orchestrator/app.py`.

## Player feedback (good / bad)

- After any tool-running job, the orchestrator appends
  `· Rate: /agent good or /agent bad <why>` to the chat reply so the
  player can grade it.
- `/agent good`, `/agent good job`, `/agent nice` mark the previous
  job good. `/agent bad <reason>` records a rejection with the reason.
- The orchestrator intercepts these prompts BEFORE the LLM ever sees
  them (see `agent/feedback.py`) and writes to
  `data/agent-feedback.jsonl`. Each row has `job_id` linking back to
  the original audit log entry.
- Build a training corpus with
  `python -m agent.training feedback --sft-out <path> --dpo-out <path>`,
  or `make feedback-export` / `make training-data`.
  SFT is built from "good" jobs; DPO needs both a good and bad rating
  on the same prompt text. Use `--report` for stats.
- Toggle the chat hint with `AGENT_ASK_FEEDBACK=0` in compose if it
  ever gets too noisy.

## Hybrid template ranker (small-model first)

`paste_template_at_player` accepts free-text in `template_id` (e.g.
`"a place for chickens to live"`); it routes through
`agent/templates/ranking.py` (lexical + local-CPU semantic + policy
reranker → confidence gate). See `docs/TEMPLATE_RANKING.md`. Don't
prompt-engineer the LLM to memorize snake_case ids — let the ranker
resolve. `search_templates` exposes the same scoring without building.

## When helping with `/agent`

- Start/rebuild with `docker compose up -d --build mc-agent` (or `make up`).
  Bumping `TOOLS_VERSION` requires this rebuild to take effect.
- If player sees "Agent offline", check `docker compose ps mc-agent`,
  `make health`, and `docker compose logs mc-agent`.
- If the plugin reports "Agent misconfigured: set AGENT_API_TOKEN" the
  Compose stack started without a token. Add it to `.env` and rebuild.
- Keep `data/plugins/NeighborhoodAgent/config.yml` as
  `orchestrator-url: http://mc-agent:8787` and `api-token: env:AGENT_API_TOKEN`.
- Bedrock names use leading `.` in all tool `player` args.
- Destructive ops require `/agent confirm <token> ...` — do not bypass.
- Prefer `fawe_*` and `build_*` tools over raw `run_command`.
- For regen/large clears: `backup_now` first, then act.
- When extending Minecraft knowledge, edit `agent/knowledge/*.md` — the
  retrieval index reloads on orchestrator restart.
- End-to-end smoke (catalog + mobs + ranker): `python3 scripts/full_validation.py`
  or `make full-validation`.
- NL prompt smoke through the real `/v1/jobs` endpoint: `make smoke` or
  see the helper pattern in `docs/TEMPLATE_RANKING.md`.

## Recommended models (Ollama)

| Model | RAM | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `qwen2.5:7b-instruct` (default) | ~5 GB | Reliable fast path on this host |
| `qwen3:8b` (fallback) | ~5 GB | Smarter in theory, but bounded by timeout |
| `llama3.1:8b` | ~5.5 GB | Solid baseline, no thinking-mode quirks |
| `qwen3:14b` / `qwen2.5:14b` | ~9 GB | Better multi-tool reasoning |
| Avoid | — | MoE / elastic models — fragment multi-step tool chains |

## Host commands

```bash
make up                                # start the stack (Ollama via profile or host)
make plugin                            # build + install the Paper plugin JAR
make health                            # GET /health from mc-agent
make logs                              # tail mc-agent + mc-lan
make smoke                             # 26 NL prompts → live LLM → /v1/jobs
docker compose up -d --build mc-agent  # rebuild orchestrator only
```

Do not publish `mc-agent` ports. It should stay private on the Compose network.
